      ],
      "text": "3.1 CHAPTER OBJECTIVES",
      "font": "TheSansSemiBold-Plain",
      "size": 9.0,
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        42.528202056884766,
        60.276031494140625,
        399.6749267578125,
        69.27603149414062
      ],
      "text": "This chapter presents a brief overview of the ﬁndings from studies of the molecular",
      "font": "TheSansSemiLight-Plain",
      "size": 9.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        42.51020431518555,
        72.27304077148438,
        261.1022033691406,
        81.27304077148438
      ],
      "text": "epidemiology of TB as it relates to contact investigation.",
      "font": "TheSansSemiLight-Plain",
      "size": 9.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        42.528202056884766,
        102.09934997558594,
        114.64521026611328,
        111.09934997558594
      ],
      "text": "3.2 BACKGROUND",
      "font": "TheSansSemiBold-Plain",
      "size": 9.0,
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        42.53720474243164,
        120.13379669189453,
        399.68377685546875,
        129.27005004882812
      ],
      "text": "M. tuberculosis Genotyping of   has been used to study the transmission dynamics of the",
      "font": "TheSansSemiLight-Italic",
      "size": 9.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        42.51920700073242,
        132.26705932617188,
        399.6390075683594,
        141.26705932617188
      ],
      "text": "organism since the early 1990s, and a number of lessons have been learnt from this approach",
      "font": "TheSansSemiLight-Plain",
      "size": 9.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        42.465206146240234,
        144.26406860351562,
        399.6839904785156,
        153.27304077148438
      ],
      "text": "(13). For certain reasons, however, including variations in the typing methods used, the",
      "font": "TheSansSemiLight-Plain",
      "size": 9.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        42.51920700073242,
        156.27005004882812,
        399.70770263671875,
        165.27304077148438
      ],
      "text": "populations examined, the deﬁnitions used and study designs, the molecular epidemiology",
      "font": "TheSansSemiLight-Plain",
      "size": 9.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        42.53379440307617,
        168.27005004882812,
        399.69866943359375,
        177.27005004882812
      ],
      "text": "of tuberculosis is difﬁcult to review systematically. This should not diminish the importance",
      "font": "TheSansSemiLight-Plain",
      "size": 9.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        42.53379440307617,
        180.26705932617188,
        401.6964416503906,
        189.26705932617188
      ],
      "text": "of the lessons learnt from use of such methods. Although a number of publications give",
      "font": "TheSansSemiLight-Plain",
      "size": 9.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        42.56979751586914,
        192.1278076171875,
        400.00482177734375,
        201.26406860351562
      ],
      "text": "M. tuberculosis the results of genotyping of   in low- and middle-income settings, only a few",
      "font": "TheSansSemiLight-Italic",
      "size": 9.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        42.83982467651367,
        204.26107788085938,
        399.5993347167969,
        213.27908325195312
      ],
      "text": "were designed to identify the features of transmission and are thus relevant to contact",
      "font": "TheSansSemiLight-Plain",
      "size": 9.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        42.56082534790039,
        216.27294921875,
        99.17381286621094,
        225.27609252929688
      ],
      "text": "investigations.",
      "font": "TheSansSemiLight-Plain",
      "size": 9.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        42.57280349731445,
        234.27294921875,
        399.7374267578125,
        243.27294921875
      ],
      "text": "Some of the applications of molecular epidemiology that, coupled with conventional",
      "font": "TheSansSemiLight-Plain",
      "size": 9.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        42.57280349731445,
        246.26995849609375,
        399.6839904785156,
        255.26995849609375
      ],
      "text": "epidemiological methods, have led to a better understanding of the distribution and dynamics",
      "font": "TheSansSemiLight-Plain",
      "size": 9.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        42.50979995727539,
        258.2669677734375,
        78.2847900390625,
        267.2669677734375
      ],
      "text": "of TB are:",
      "font": "TheSansSemiLight-Plain",
      "size": 9.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        42.50979995727539,
        276.2669677734375,
        218.1178436279297,
        285.2669677734375
      ],
      "text": "• identiﬁcation or conﬁrmation of outbreaks,",
      "font": "TheSansSemiLight-Plain",
      "size": 9.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        42.518802642822266,
        294.2669677734375,
        249.81582641601562,
        303.2669677734375
      ],
      "text": "• identiﬁcation of sites at which transmission occurs,",
      "font": "TheSansSemiLight-Plain",
      "size": 9.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        42.52780532836914,
        312.2669677734375,
        251.05642700195312,
        321.2759704589844
      ],
      "text": "• identiﬁcation of characteristics of TB disseminators,",
      "font": "TheSansSemiLight-Plain",
      "size": 9.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        42.52639389038086,
        330.2758483886719,
        399.5655822753906,
        339.2758483886719
      ],
      "text": "• characteristics of people at increased risk for acquiring TB infection and for rapid progression",
      "font": "TheSansSemiLight-Plain",
      "size": 9.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        50.89639663696289,
        342.2728576660156,
        72.0823974609375,
        351.2728576660156
      ],
      "text": "to TB,",
      "font": "TheSansSemiLight-Plain",
      "size": 9.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        42.39139938354492,
        360.2728576660156,
        204.13037109375,
        369.2728576660156
      ],
      "text": "• detection of unsuspected transmission,",
      "font": "TheSansSemiLight-Plain",
      "size": 9.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        42.4004020690918,
        378.2728576660156,
        228.99745178222656,
        387.2728576660156
      ],
      "text": "• determination of the potential for reinfection,",
      "font": "TheSansSemiLight-Plain",
      "size": 9.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        42.40940475463867,
        396.2728576660156,
        239.20343017578125,
        405.2728576660156
      ],
      "text": "• detection of laboratory cross-contamination and",
      "font": "TheSansSemiLight-Plain",
      "size": 9.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        42.41840744018555,
        414.2728576660156,
        313.2283630371094,
        423.2728576660156
      ],
      "text": "• evaluation of TB control activities designed to prevent transmission.",
      "font": "TheSansSemiLight-Plain",
      "size": 9.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        42.42741012573242,
        444.0991516113281,
        152.54241943359375,
        453.0991516113281
      ],
      "text": "3.3 SUMMARY OF FINDINGS",
      "font": "TheSansSemiBold-Plain",
      "size": 9.0,
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        42.4364128112793,
        462.2698669433594,
        399.8074645996094,
        471.2788391113281
      ],
      "text": "Perhaps the most relevant lesson from molecular epidemiology for contact investigation is",
      "font": "TheSansSemiLight-Plain",
      "size": 9.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        42.63351058959961,
        474.13677978515625,
        399.87017822265625,
        483.2730407714844
      ],
      "text": "M. tuberculosis that substantial transmission of   may occur outside households, such as in",
      "font": "TheSansSemiLight-Italic",
      "size": 9.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        42.69649887084961,
        486.2700500488281,
        399.8341979980469,
        495.2700500488281
      ],
      "text": "social settings like bars and in multi-resident housing such as hotels and shelters for the",
      "font": "TheSansSemiLight-Plain",
      "size": 9.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        42.669498443603516,
        498.26702880859375,
        400.2573547363281,
        507.26702880859375
      ],
      "text": "homeless (14–16). Thus, contact investigations should not focus exclusively on the household,",
      "font": "TheSansSemiLight-Plain",
      "size": 9.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        42.6515007019043,
        510.2640075683594,
        399.7174072265625,
        519.2730712890625
      ],
      "text": "depending on the circumstances. Molecular epidemiology has also been used to identify",
      "font": "TheSansSemiLight-Plain",
      "size": 9.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        42.543514251708984,
        522.2700805664062,
        399.69927978515625,
        531.2700805664062
      ],
      "text": "groups at increased risk for acquiring infection and rapid progression to active TB. PLHIV",
      "font": "TheSansSemiLight-Plain",
      "size": 9.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        42.53451156616211,
        534.2670288085938,
        400.1329650878906,
        543.2688598632812
      ],
      "text": "obviously fall into this category, but homelessness and substance abuse are also risk factors.",
      "font": "TheSansSemiLight-Plain",
      "size": 9.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        42.590091705322266,
        546.265869140625,
        400.2226257324219,
        555.265869140625
      ],
      "text": "In addition, in population-based molecular epidemiological studies in British Columbia,",
      "font": "TheSansSemiLight-Plain",
      "size": 9.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        42.61709213256836,
        558.2628784179688,
        399.7818603515625,
        567.2628784179688
      ],
      "text": "Canada, The Netherlands and San Francisco, USA, 12–17% of new cases were the result of",
      "font": "TheSansSemiLight-Plain",
      "size": 9.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        42.61709213256836,
        570.2598876953125,
        399.7457275390625,
        579.2778930664062
      ],
      "text": "transmission from smear-negative, culture-positive cases (17–19). Thus, although a large",
      "font": "TheSansSemiLight-Plain",
      "size": 9.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        42.58109664916992,
        582.2703857421875,
        399.5799865722656,
        591.27490234375
      ],
      "text": "majority of cases result from contact with a smear-positive case, smear-negative cases can",
      "font": "TheSansSemiLight-Plain",
      "size": 9.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        42.406002044677734,
        594.2673950195312,
        143.39498901367188,
        603.2673950195312
      ],
      "text": "also transmit the disease.",
      "font": "TheSansSemiLight-Plain",
      "size": 9.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        217.24310302734375,
        651.97265625,
        224.96810913085938,
        659.47265625
      ],
      "text": "24",
      "font": "TheSansSemiBold-Plain",
      "size": 7.5,
      "type": "heading"
    }
  ]
